 "notes": [
  "Weekdays are two hours after work. Fridays and Saturdays are counted as three. A day over that shows a full bar.",
  "All 67 GRE chapters would take about 45 hours. That does not fit, so 45 of them are planned before Nov 26 and the other 22 are parked. If you retake, press Re-plan remaining on the GRE page.",
  "Check the TOEFL first. Harvard asks for it unless your bachelor's was 3 years in person, taught in English, in a listed country, and KSA is not on that list.",
  "Nov 28 to 30 hold three small abstracts you marked as planning. Skip any of them, nothing depends on them.",
  "Dec 15 to 27 is kept light on purpose: retake seats, a TOEFL backup, and rest.",
  "Exact essay lengths are only inside the application. Day 1 is to copy them into Notes.",
  "Harvard's pages were read through a summarising tool. Please glance at the live page for exact wording before relying on a number."
 ]
